{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_the_decisions_we_need_from_you_open_decisions_24_oct_2026", "label": "The Decisions We Need From You (open decisions, 24 Oct 2026)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "title", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Puts the audit's 25 questions to AMPM with the choices, the default assumed so that design could continue and what changes with each answer; Tier 1 blocks sign-off of the screen designs and the data model, Tier 2 must be answered before building starts, Tier 3 can wait for the planning phases."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumptions_taken_md", "label": "assumptions-taken.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Answer sheet footnote", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every answer feeds the assumptions sheet; the decision register in the developer package lists which assumptions each answer confirms or replaces."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q1_responsive_installable_website_with_offline_reading_on_the_wedding_day", "label": "Assumed Q1: responsive installable website with offline reading on the wedding day", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Native apps roughly double the front-end work and need app-store accounts while a website reaches every phone the day it is published; staff use phones inside hotel ballrooms with poor signal, so the answer also decides how much offline behaviour is built. Choosing native apps adds builds to the estimate but leaves the server unchanged."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q2_both_payment_paths_online_gateway_and_bank_transfer_after_ampm_invites_the_client", "label": "Assumed Q2: both payment paths, online gateway and bank transfer, after AMPM invites the client", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Why note says AMPM creates every account and the specification describes a payment journey; both hold if AMPM invites first. A gateway merchant account takes one to two weeks to open; bank transfer only would remove the gateway from Phase 1."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q3_one_time_fixed_term_subscription_sales_granted_trial_curated_demo_with_prices_hidden", "label": "Assumed Q3: one-time fixed-term subscription, Sales-granted trial, curated demo with prices hidden", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recurring billing needs renewals, failed-payment handling and reminders, a sizeable piece of work; the demo and trial appear only in the Why note so they had to be defined. Demo content is a data choice, not a design change."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q4_margin_model_with_a_client_facing_amount_and_a_separate_internal_cost", "label": "Assumed Q4: margin model with a client-facing amount and a separate internal cost", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Designed for the strictest case so every money screen works whichever model AMPM picks: the internal side never leaves the server; a transparent fee only adds a visible fee line; removing online milestone payment turns the Pay button into bank-transfer instructions."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q5_owner_approver_and_viewer_client_roles_with_one_approval_per_decision", "label": "Assumed Q5: Owner, Approver and Viewer client roles with one approval per decision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In many weddings the parents pay and the couple designs, so the portal must show money to the right people and nobody else; staff may record a phone decision only with a note or document attached."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q6_the_eleven_spec_roles_stand_with_scoped_cost_and_margin_visibility", "label": "Assumed Q6: the eleven SPEC roles stand with scoped cost and margin visibility", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Internal cost visible to Super Admin and Finance everywhere, the Wedding Project Manager on their own weddings, the Vendor Coordinator for vendor costs and the Hotel team for hotel costs; roles are configuration, so changing them changes a table, not the design."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q7_private_rsvp_link_per_household_with_the_guest_list_loaded_first", "label": "Assumed Q7: private RSVP link per household with the guest list loaded first", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One link for everyone forces guests to find themselves in a list, creating duplicates and letting people see other families; a private link per household avoids both but means the list must exist before invitations go out. Meal preference required, allergies optional, extra members within an allowance set by the family."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q8_identity_documents_off_by_default_never_aadhaar_deleted_30_days_after_checkout", "label": "Assumed Q8: identity documents off by default, never Aadhaar, deleted 30 days after checkout", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Identity documents are the most sensitive data in the system, Indian rules restrict storing Aadhaar numbers and a breach would be serious; passport, voter ID or driving licence only, seen by named RSVP staff and hospitality at check-in, every view logged."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q9_seasonal_rate_card_with_line_items_availability_answered_per_enquiry_media_only_with_consent", "label": "Assumed Q9: seasonal rate card with line items, availability answered per enquiry, media only with consent", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The specification's data model had no place to put a price, so a rate card per season was designed with room rate per category, venue rental, per-plate minimums and taxes, each verified on a date by a named person; a live availability calendar would be a large addition; existing data imported from spreadsheets."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q10_demo_and_trial_full_hotel_assistance_online_payment_and_website_editing_all_in_phase_1", "label": "Assumed Q10: demo and trial, full hotel assistance, online payment and website editing all in Phase 1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 1 Q10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exceptions letting a function go live with a check unmet authorised by the Wedding Project Manager or the Super Admin; anything removed moves to a later phase and shortens Phase 1."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q11_email_whatsapp_and_sms_through_business_providers", "label": "Assumed Q11: email, WhatsApp and SMS through business providers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 2 Q11", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WhatsApp business verification and template approval take two to six weeks and SMS needs a DLT registration of two to four weeks, so registrations should start early."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q12_ampm_team_edits_the_public_website_in_a_simple_editor", "label": "Assumed Q12: AMPM team edits the public website in a simple editor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 2 Q12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A simple editor for pages, destinations and showcase items, with analytics and a low-friction bot check on forms."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q13_email_and_password_for_clients_authenticator_app_for_staff_private_links_for_guests", "label": "Assumed Q13: email and password for clients, authenticator app for staff, private links for guests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 2 Q13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Clients get an optional phone code; nobody can register themselves."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q14_indian_cloud_region_with_a_second_region_copy_15_minute_data_loss_limit_4_hour_recovery", "label": "Assumed Q14: Indian cloud region with a second-region copy, 15-minute data loss limit, 4-hour recovery", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 2 Q14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cloud and provider accounts opened in AMPM's name."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q15_sizing_50_staff_40_concurrent_weddings_1500_guests_per_wedding_500_hotels_2_tb_media", "label": "Assumed Q15 sizing: 50 staff, 40 concurrent weddings, 1500 guests per wedding, 500 hotels, 2 TB media", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 2 Q15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cost estimate depends on these numbers."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q16_indian_rupees_english_with_a_second_language_ready_guest_portal_gst_invoices_from_the_platform", "label": "Assumed Q16: Indian rupees, English with a second-language-ready guest portal, GST invoices from the platform", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 2 Q16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q17_retention_closed_leads_2_years_guest_data_1_year_after_closing_identity_documents_30_days_after_checkout", "label": "Assumed Q17 retention: closed leads 2 years, guest data 1 year after closing, identity documents 30 days after checkout", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 2 Q17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Consent notices on the enquiry form and the guest portal in wording AMPM approves."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q18_multi_hotel_weddings_and_venues_outside_the_database_allowed", "label": "Assumed Q18: multi-hotel weddings and venues outside the database allowed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A wedding can use a main hotel and overflow hotels and a function can be at a venue outside the database."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q19_room_blocks_per_hotel_category_and_dates_with_children_counted_as_occupants", "label": "Assumed Q19: room blocks per hotel, category and dates with children counted as occupants", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Blocks come from the contract and guests are allocated against the block."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q20_tracked_requests_with_a_conversation_no_live_chat", "label": "Assumed Q20: tracked requests with a conversation, no live chat", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A client asks a question or raises a change as a tracked request that the team answers."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q21_change_request_lifecycle_submitted_under_review_accepted_or_rejected_implemented_new_version_on_an_accepted_change", "label": "Assumed Q21 change-request lifecycle: submitted, under review, accepted or rejected, implemented; new version on an accepted change", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An accepted change to something already approved produces a new version for a new approval."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q22_no_vendor_or_hotel_logins_in_this_project", "label": "Assumed Q22: no vendor or hotel logins in this project", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q22", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A vendor portal can be added later without changing the vendor records."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q23_twelve_months_read_only_client_access_after_closure_then_archive", "label": "Assumed Q23: twelve months read-only client access after closure, then archive", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Logins are removed at archive; nothing is deleted."}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q24_short_feedback_form_and_archived_state_keeping_every_record", "label": "Assumed Q24: short feedback form and archived state keeping every record", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q24", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumed_q25_material_change_is_a_10_percent_budget_move_or_a_date_or_venue_change_thresholds_as_settings", "label": "Assumed Q25: material change is a 10 percent budget move or a date or venue change, thresholds as settings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Tier 3 Q25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The specification says material changes must flag budgets, contracts, tasks and the run-of-show but never defines material."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_review_open_decisions_the_decisions_we_need_from_you_open_decisions_24_oct_2026", "target": "docs_review_open_decisions_assumptions_taken_md", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/review/open-decisions.md", "source_location": "Answer sheet", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_review_open_decisions_the_decisions_we_need_from_you_open_decisions_24_oct_2026", "target": "docs_requirements_audit_amp